  "scope": "Group-successor registration inside existing branch settlement: prefix and preparation routing, next-plan assembly and graph proof, memory conflict/write ordering and SQLite record/encoding/deadline/quota/write coordination.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen registration bodies retain original authority loading and next-plan assembly; codecs, binding evaluation and graph proof remain shared, not migrated registration coordination. The frozen next-plan path keeps the original test-only helper.",
    "Native entry still owns bounded/admitted plans, original reservations and selection of initial versus capture re-entry. This is not an arbitrary-input-safe evaluator or a new standalone runtime.",
    "The 168 memory cases span twelve original group shapes and fourteen low-level scenarios; the 288 SQLite cases span those shapes and twenty-four scenarios, not all 70 host operations.",
    "Memory retains non-Done prefix bypass, preparation-fault receipts, conflict short-circuit and insertion before late owner lookup. Trusted callback failure/unwind preserves prior side effects without retry or compensation.",
    "SQLite retains streaming decode fault precedence, record bound, four encoding order, signed deadline, incremental quota and effect/dispatch/plan/link writes inside the caller's transaction. There is no new dispatch admission or watermark reservation.",
    "Corrupt fixtures are not supported checkpoints. A disposable view supplies a wrong later storage class to probe earlier decode failure; production STRICT tables are unchanged and fixture checks are restored before invoking the code.",
    "Twelve memory and twelve durable complete shape checks reuse the original evaluator, including tail/capture/multi-capture/conditional forms. Durable final receipts reopen without redispatch or additional reservations.",
    "Ten public cases inject effect/dispatch/plan/link failures and deferred-commit failure, then reopen and explicitly retry. Last-member settlement and all successor writes roll back together, without completed-cache publication or duplicate successors.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, exported-source execution, full host-neutral durable recovery, power-loss, disk-full, multi-host race or throughput evidence is claimed."
  ],
